This file summarizes changes made between B-Tree Filer versions 5.40
and 5.41. It is of interest primarily to Fast Update Plan subscribers.

New Features and Changes
---------------------------------------------------------------------
This version of B-Tree Filer has been released to clear up some out-
standing bugs, to provide compatibility for fileblocks created with
B-Tree Filer for C, and also to provide the DBIMPEXP unit to convert
data between Filer fileblocks and dBase data and memo files.

WARNING: if you are using network B-Tree Filer under NetWare and are
         using shell versions 3.31 and 3.32 (the shells for MSDOS
         6.0), be aware that Novell reintroduced a bug that used to
         exist in shells earlier than version 3.22 (the 'reading a
         locked record does not fail' bug). See the discussion in
         the READ.ME file and in the manual.

FILER
  - MaxNrOfWorkstations is now a typed constant, and can be altered
    if required _before_ calling BTInitIsam.
  - error 10065 (class 2) is raised whenever an attempt is made to
    write to a fileblock opened in read-only mode.
  - a new typed constant TestNetExistance has been introduced. If
    set to true (the default) then BTInitIsam will do an internal
    check to see whether the network specified in ExpectedNet can be
    found. If false, no check for the network is made.
  - a new constant InheritFileHandles has been introduced. This
    defines whether any child processes receive the open fileblock
    handles. If False (the default) then child processes will not
    inherit the fileblock handles, if True then they will. Note
    however, that child processes will *not* inherit any of the
    B-Tree Filer data structures.
  - ExtendHandles has been changed slightly, in that you can now
    specify a number less than 20.

BASESUPP
  - various enhancements have been made to bring together DPMI and
    Windows handling.

NUMKEYS
  - new routines have been added: ByteToKey, KeyToByte, CStyleNumKey
    PascalStyleNumKey, CStyleDescendingKey to mimic the binary to key
    routines that B-Tree Filer for C provides.

MSORT
  - for various reasons MSORT was not very efficient in protected
    mode (either Windows or DPMI). A new unit has been written called
    MSORTP. It has a similar interface to MSORT, but works exclusively
    in pmode. MSORT will now only compile in real mode. MSORTP is
    found on the BONUS diskette.

DBIMPEXP
  - a new unit that facilitates converting data from dBase data and
    memo files to B-Tree Filer fileblocks, and vice versa. Full
    details are available in the text file DBIMPEXP.DOC.


New Features and Changes to BONUS Files
---------------------------------------------------------------------
NETBONUS
  - now incorporates all the network specific BONUS files, including
    the previously separate NETBIOS, NETPRN, NETTEST and TRAFFIC
    files.

NETBIOS2
  - now supports Windows and DPMI modes


Bugs Fixed
---------------------------------------------------------------------
FILER
  - NovellUnlockRecord used wrong record length (seemed to only make
    a difference in certain cases)
  - BTLockFileBlock would return IsamError=10330 but with IsamOk=true
  - under certain circumstances Filer would allow a write to a
    readonly fileblock
  - in pmode if a bad index number was passed to certain routines a
    GPF would be generated before a programming error could be
    reported
  - BTNextKey and BTPrevKey had some problems with a fileblock opened
    in readonly mode

BROWSER
  - numerous changes have been made to clear up the UseReadLock
    handling, and lock error handling
  - the scrollbar slider was never drawn with the correct attribute

IPXSPX, IPXSPXD
  - numerous changes have been made to clear up bugs introduced in
    versions 5.23 and 5.40
  - a Move was made to an un-dereferenced pointer in IPXListen

WINDPMI
  - there was one statement that assumed $X+ (the default for Windows
    targets), the default for DPMI targets is however $X-

NETWARE
  - GetPrinterStatus is not supported under NetWare 3.x, the function
    now returns the NetWare error code

NETBIOSD
  - the Windows NetBIOS real-mode callback would corrupt the real-mode
    stack

EMSHEAP
  - calling ExitEMSHeap when ManualInitEMSHeap was defined would break
    the exit procedure chain

MSORT
  - when compiling with $T+, a 'type mismatch' error would be
    generated; the unit now has an explicit $T-

OOFILER (bonus)
  - the ModifyRecord and DeleteRecord methods treated null keys in a
    different fashion

OBROWSE (bonus)
  - various fixes have been made to solve highlight bar problems

